;;; mf-c8.scm -- Proposition 3.17, uniqueness: |nu| is unique, and u is unique |nu|-almost everywhere.
;;; Agent M-F, 2026-10-29.  DESTINATION: theorem-library/complex-measure-polar.scm (after mf-c7).  Library: measure.
;;; Helper prefix: mfu-.  Load window: after mf-c7.scm.
;;; Route: for two solutions (mu1, u1), (mu2, u2), rho = mu1 + mu2 dominates both; with densities h1, h2 the real and
;;; imaginary parts of int_A u_i dmu_i are int_A h_i Re u_i drho, int_A h_i Im u_i drho; equal for every A, so
;;; h1 Re u1 = h2 Re u2 and h1 Im u1 = h2 Im u2 rho-a.e.; taking moduli h1 = h2 rho-a.e., so mu1 = mu2, and u1 = u2 off a
;;; rho-null set and off {h1 = 0}, which is mu1-null.  (The notes' route through a density of rho w.r.t. mu is the same
;;; idea; this one does not need the hypothesis that mu1, mu2 have the null sets of nu.)

   ; KIT-9 link skipping, opt-in per file (integrator, 2026-10-29)

